        <selectionEntry name="Indicium Malefica (Cybertheurgic Rite)" id="c567-2b23-551e-d6d2" collective="true" hidden="false" import="true" page="151" publicationId="4934-46f7-208b-b4af" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d3dd-88c1-7d41-fb95" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="4cea-7b84-61f3-f85c" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Indicium Malefica  (Cybertheurgic Rite)" id="3f69-fe41-5ee7-0c1a" hidden="false" page="151" publicationId="4934-46f7-208b-b4af" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">A Cybertheurgist with this Cybertheurgic Rite may use it instead of making a Shooting Attack in the controlling player&apos;s Shooting phase. When they do, the controlling player may select a single enemy unit and roll a D6 for each model (excluding model with the Vehicle Unit Type) in that unit that is within 6&quot; of the Cybertheurgist model. For each result that equals or beats that model&apos;s Save characteristic, that model&apos;s unit suffers one Wound, allocated by the Active player. Saving Throws and Damage Mitigation rolls can be taken against this Wound as normal. The controlling player then rolls a D6 for each affected model with the Vehicle Unit Type. For each result of 6, one affected model with the Vehicle Unit Type suffers a Crew Stunned result from the Vehicle Damage table.

The Cybertheurgist may choose to make a Cybertheurgy check before using this Cybertheurgic Rite. If successful, every enemy model within 6&quot; of the Cybertheurgist model is affected instead.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Ruinous Cybernetica" id="c7f4-8f4e-f31d-5323" hidden="true" import="true" page="151" publicationId="4934-46f7-208b-b4af" type="upgrade">
